const faqs=[['What is the FIRE number?','A common financial independence rule of thumb divides annual retirement spending by an assumed annual withdrawal rate. For example, $80,000 in spending at 4% results in a $2 million target.'],['Is the 4% rule guaranteed?','No. It is a planning heuristic, not a guarantee. Market conditions, retirement length, tax treatment and spending changes can affect sustainability.'],['What does the growth assumption mean?','Enter an annual nominal investment growth assumption and an inflation estimate. The calculator derives a real growth rate and models a steady savings contribution in current purchasing power.'],['Does this include pensions, Social Security or taxes on investments?','No. Government benefits, pension payments, investment taxes, fees, and future lifestyle changes are excluded.']];
