<BaseLayout title="Couples FIRE Calculator: Financial Independence Roadmap | DollarAngle" description="Free Couples FIRE calculator. Set joint income, household spending, invested assets, savings and withdrawal rate to estimate financial independence targets and timelines.">
<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />
<div class="container page"><nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> › <a href="/tools">Money Tools</a> › Couples FIRE Roadmap</nav>
<header class="intro"><p class="kicker">FREE COUPLES FINANCIAL INDEPENDENCE TOOL</p><h1>Couples' FIRE Roadmap: <span>When Could You Be Financially Independent?</span></h1><p>Financial independence is more than a savings balance. Model your joint earnings, spending, withdrawal assumption and investment growth to see what your timeline might look like.</p></header>
<CouplesFireRoadmap />
<article class="guide"><h2>How to calculate a couples' FIRE number</h2><p>The basic FIRE target divides annual household spending by your chosen withdrawal rate. For example, a $75,000 annual budget divided by 4% gives a $1,875,000 target. You can change the withdrawal rate to explore a more cautious or more aggressive assumption.</p>
<h2>How the retirement timeline is estimated</h2><p>The calculator starts with existing invested assets, adds your combined monthly income less spending plus any manual savings adjustment, and applies a constant inflation-adjusted investment return. It then estimates when the portfolio crosses the stated FIRE target. This simplified projection assumes contributions stay constant in today's money and excludes market fluctuations.</p>
<h2>How couples can use this plan together</h2><p>Compare different lifestyles and savings amounts rather than treating one forecast as a promise. Discuss housing, healthcare, dependents, emergency savings, pension benefits, taxes and how each partner wants to spend their time once work becomes optional.</p>
<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>{faqs.map(([q,a])=><details><summary>{q}</summary><p>{a}</p></details>)}
<h2>Related DollarAngle tools</h2><p><a href="/tools/mine-yours-ours-budget-calculator">Build your Mine, Yours, Ours budget →</a> <a href="/tools/couples-debt-payoff-calculator">Plan your debt payoff →</a></p>
<p class="note">Educational illustration only, not investment or retirement advice. Inflation, taxes, fees, variable returns, sequence-of-returns risk and benefit eligibility can materially change results. No withdrawal rate can guarantee financial independence.</p></article></div>
</BaseLayout>
